# Web app

`apps/web` is a Vite + React + TypeScript SPA. It renders projections and sends user-authorized commands. It is not a second backend.

## Data access

- Use `supabase-js` with the publishable key and the user session.
- Read projections. Do not treat the browser as the place that maintains read models.
- Append an event from the client only when RLS can authorize that insert alone.
- If a command needs branching, a model, or more than one stream, call `services/agent`. Do not reimplement that command in the client.

## UI

- Functional components. Shared data access goes in hooks next to the feature.
- A proposal is shown as proposed, verified, approved, or rejected. The UI never marks a proposal approved without the human action that appends the approval event.
- Do not import an LLM SDK, Koog, or a service-role client.

```tsx
// ❌ client writes the read model
await supabase.from("rules").update({ body }).eq("id", id);

// ✅ client appends a fact the member is allowed to record
await supabase.from("events").insert({ org_id, stream_id, stream_type: "rule", version, event_type: "RuleUpdated", schema_version: 1, payload, actor_id });
```
